---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import { SOCIAL, MRALABS_URL } from "../lib/profile";
---

<Base
  title="About — Emrah Yumuk"
  description="Software engineer building products end to end, from architecture to cloud, with a small fleet of AI coding agents."
  promptPath="~/about"
>
  <p class="cmd-line">$ cat about.md</p>
  <h1 class="page-title">about</h1>
  <div class="prose">
    <p>
      Software engineer. I started tinkering with the web in 2005, the year I
      started university, and never quite stopped building things for it.
    </p>
    <p>
      These days I build products end to end: the architecture, the backend, the
      frontend, the cloud underneath. Most of the actual typing is done by AI
      coding agents I run in parallel; I design the system, keep the quality
      gates up, and review everything that ships. It took fifteen-plus years of
      building software the manual way to get here, and I suspect that's exactly
      why it works.
    </p>
    <p>
      <a href={MRALABS_URL} target="_blank" rel="noopener">mralabs</a>{" "}
      is where all of this lives. A one-person software lab: my own products, at my
      own pace.
    </p>
    <p>
      Metal in my headphones most of the day, coding or not. Away from the
      screen it's craft beer (I used to brew my own, and probably will again)
      and pour-over coffee that takes longer than it should. Istanbul, Kadıköy
      side.
    </p>
  </div>
  <p class="mono contact">
    <a href={SOCIAL.github} target="_blank" rel="noopener">github</a>
    <span class="sep">·</span>
    <a href={SOCIAL.linkedin} target="_blank" rel="noopener">linkedin</a>
    <span class="sep">·</span>
    <a href={SOCIAL.untappd} target="_blank" rel="noopener">untappd</a>
    <span class="sep">·</span>
    <a href={SOCIAL.rym} target="_blank" rel="noopener">rym</a>
    {/* · email — pending a proper site address */}
  </p>
</Base>

<style>
  .contact {
    margin-top: 2.2rem;
  }
  .sep {
    color: var(--muted);
    margin-inline: 0.4rem;
  }
</style>
